UNKNOWN OPERATOR

  × Nash uses a different name for the “not equal” operator:
   ╭─[Main.nash:1:1]
 1 │ name = other
   · ────
   ╰────
  help: Switch to (/=) instead. Our (/=) operator is supposed to look like a real “not
        equal” sign (≠). I hope that history will remember (!=) as a weird and temporary
        choice.
